msgctxt "Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Lines.TLine1"
msgid "<html>\n"
"<p>Lossless transmission line with characteristic impedance Z0 and transmission delay TD The lossless transmission line TLine1 is a two Port. Both port branches consist of a resistor with characteristic impedance Z0 and a controlled voltage source that takes into consideration the transmission delay TD. For further details see [<a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Electrical.Analog.UsersGuide.References\">Branin1967</a>]. The model parameters can be derived from inductance and capacitance per length (L&#39; resp. C&#39;), i. e. Z0 = sqrt(L&#39;/C&#39;) and TD = sqrt(L&#39;*C&#39;)*length_of_line. Resistance R&#39; and conductance C&#39; per meter are assumed to be zero.</p>\n"
"\n"
"<p><strong>References:</strong>\n"
"   [<a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Electrical.Analog.UsersGuide.References\">Branin1967</a>],\n"
"   [<a href=\"modelica://Modelica.Electrical.Analog.UsersGuide.References\">Hoefer1985</a>]</p>\n"
"</html>"
